# Shell scripts are piped straight into `bash` from raw.githubusercontent.com —
# a CRLF copy dies at the first `case` ("syntax error near unexpected token").
# Pin them to LF so no Windows checkout can commit a broken installer.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The chat page's assets are generated by `bun run build` with LF and committed
# as generated. Without this, `core.autocrlf` checks them out as CRLF and every
# build on Windows leaves the tree dirty over a difference that is not in the
# file — and `build.rs` digests whatever bytes are on disk, so the checkout
# should be the bytes the build writes. Named by extension, not by folder: a
# wildcard would also cover `favicon.png`, and normalising a PNG corrupts it.
webrain-cli/assets/*.js text eol=lf
webrain-cli/assets/*.css text eol=lf
webrain-cli/assets/*.html text eol=lf
